## Configuration

| Setting | Env var | Default | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|---------|
| Hook retry limit | `HOOK_RETRY` | 3 | Max Job failures before "Retry limit exceeded" |
| Hook CPU limit | `HOOKS_CONTAINER_LIMITS_CPU` | 1000m | Local hook pod |
| Hook memory limit | `HOOKS_CONTAINER_LIMITS_MEMORY` | 1Gi | Local hook pod |
| Hook CPU request | `HOOKS_CONTAINER_REQUESTS_CPU` | 100m | Local hook pod |
| Hook memory request | `HOOKS_CONTAINER_REQUESTS_MEMORY` | 150Mi | Local hook pod |
| AAP URL | `AAP_URL` | — | Cluster-wide AAP base URL |
| AAP token Secret | `AAP_TOKEN_SECRET_NAME` | — | Cluster-wide token Secret name |
| AAP timeout | `AAP_TIMEOUT` | — | Default poll timeout (seconds) |

ForkliftController CR fields `aap_url`, `aap_token_secret_name`, `aap_timeout` map to these env vars via the operator.

---

## Error Patterns

- Hook validation sets conditions without failing reconcile.
- Missing Hook at execution time → step error "Hook not found."
- AAP misconfiguration → step error with descriptive message, step marked completed.
- Local Job failures are terminal after retry limit; migration continues to report the error on the step.

---

## Frontend Relevance

- Hooks configured in Plan create/edit — each VM can reference pre/post hooks (`spec.vms[].hooks[]`).
- Hook CRD conditions (`InvalidImage`, `InvalidPlaybook`, `InvalidHookExecute`) should surface as validation errors on the Hooks list/details pages.
- AAP hooks: UI must support `spec.aap` fields (`jobTemplateId`, optional `url`, `tokenSecret`, `timeout`) and explain cluster vs per-hook connection requirements.
- Local hooks: `image` required; `playbook` optional (image default CMD may run without a playbook).
- Hook execution visible in per-VM migration pipeline as `PreHook`/`PostHook` steps.
- Default hook runner image: `quay.io/konveyor/hook-runner` (or `quay.io/kubev2v/hook-runner`).
- Type: `V1beta1Hook` from `@forklift-ui/types`.
